<h1>Security</h1>

<p>
  We understand that many users place a high level of trust in OpenGyoza and
  the tools we build. We apply best practices and focus on security to make
  sure we can maintain the trust of the community.
</p>
<p>
  We deeply appreciate any effort to disclose vulnerabilities responsibly.
</p>
<p>
  If you would like to report a vulnerability, please see our
  <a href="https://github.com/opengyoza/opengyoza/blob/main/SECURITY.md">security policy</a>
  for contact details and PGP information.
</p>
<p>
  If you aren't reporting a security sensitive vulnerability, please
  open an issue on the standard <a href="https://github.com/opengyoza/opengyoza">GitHub</a>
  repository.
</p>
